<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masaniello</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1620–1647</span> · Also known as Tommaso Aniello</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masaniello, born Tommaso Aniello, was a Neapolitan fisherman who led the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> against Spanish rule and a new tax on fruit in July 1647. For about ten days he dominated the city and negotiated with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, but he grew erratic and was murdered on 16 July 1647. The revolt continued and led to the short-lived Neapolitan Republic of 1647–1648.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masaniello.jpg" alt="Masaniello" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Onofrio Palumbo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Onofrio_Palumbo_-_Masaniello.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
